      "data": {
        "nodeType": "binding-free-energy",
        "label": "Binding Free Energy",
        "icon": "zap",
        "color": "amber",
        "inputs": [
          {
            "id": "complexes",
            "name": "Complexes",
            "type": "array",
            "required": false,
            "description": "Docked PROTEIN-LIGAND complexes to score (uni-gbsa path). Each pose's ligand (``pose_uri``) is paired with its receptor (``target_pdb_uri``) and run through MM-GB/PBSA. The ligand pose must be an RDKit-parseable SDF (``pose_format: sdf``) — feed output from an SDF-emitting docking model (diffdock / gnina / sigmadock / smina / surfdock / dynamicbind); pdbqt (autodock-vina) and pdb poses lack bond orders and are rejected. Each input emits one BINDING_FREE_ENERGY estimate (ΔG_bind + decomposition). Supply EITHER `complexes` (uni-gbsa) OR `trajectories` (g_mmpbsa) per node.\n",
            "tooltip": "Docked PROTEIN-LIGAND complexes to score (uni-gbsa path). Each pose's ligand (``pose_uri``) is paired with its receptor (``target_pdb_uri``) and run through MM-GB/PBSA. The ligand pose must be an RDKit-parseable SDF (``pose_format: sdf``) — feed output from an SDF-emitting docking model (diffdock / gnina / sigmadock / smina / surfdock / dynamicbind); pdbqt (autodock-vina) and pdb poses lack bond orders and are rejected. Each input emits one BINDING_FREE_ENERGY estimate (ΔG_bind + decomposition). Supply EITHER `complexes` (uni-gbsa) OR `trajectories` (g_mmpbsa) per node.\n",
            "expectedStandardType": "DOCKED_STRUCTURE",
            "providedStandardType": "DOCKED_STRUCTURE"
          },
          {
            "id": "trajectories",
            "name": "Trajectories",
            "type": "array",
            "required": false,
            "description": "Completed protein-ligand COMPLEX MD trajectories to score with end-point MM-PBSA (g_mmpbsa path) — wire directly from molecular-dynamics/gromacs (the `complexes` path). The adapter takes the GROMACS trajectory (``.xtc``) + run-input topology (``.tpr``) from ``properties.full_system_*`` and SYNTHESIZES the two files the worker also requires: a receptor/ligand index (``.ndx``, built from atom-count ranges — protein count from the viewer PDB, ligand count from ``properties.ligand.natoms``) and a static APBS parameter file (``.mdp``). The g_mmpbsa worker then computes ΔG_bind (van der Waals + electrostatic MM, polar and apolar solvation). Requires gromacs complex metadata (``properties.trajectory_viewer_pdb`` + ``ligand.natoms``). Supply EITHER `trajectories` (g_mmpbsa) OR `complexes` (uni-gbsa) per node.\n",
            "tooltip": "Completed protein-ligand COMPLEX MD trajectories to score with end-point MM-PBSA (g_mmpbsa path) — wire directly from molecular-dynamics/gromacs (the `complexes` path). The adapter takes the GROMACS trajectory (``.xtc``) + run-input topology (``.tpr``) from ``properties.full_system_*`` and SYNTHESIZES the two files the worker also requires: a receptor/ligand index (``.ndx``, built from atom-count ranges — protein count from the viewer PDB, ligand count from ``properties.ligand.natoms``) and a static APBS parameter file (``.mdp``). The g_mmpbsa worker then computes ΔG_bind (van der Waals + electrostatic MM, polar and apolar solvation). Requires gromacs complex metadata (``properties.trajectory_viewer_pdb`` + ``ligand.natoms``). Supply EITHER `trajectories` (g_mmpbsa) OR `complexes` (uni-gbsa) per node.\n",
            "expectedStandardType": "MD_TRAJECTORY",
            "providedStandardType": "MD_TRAJECTORY"
          }
        ],
